  "name": "Woodcutting and Woodworking recipes are learned as the skill reaches them",
  "contract": "Neither trade has a trainer. The client's SkillLineAbility marks every recipe of both trainer-taught and no creature in the realm carries a row for either skill, so the recipes are learned with the skill itself by mod-woodworking's script, gated by the skill the client declares for each recipe: its MinSkillLineRank where that is above 1 (the four Refine spells above Forestwood, at 65, 125, 165 and 230) and its TrivialSkillLineRankLow otherwise (the wood tiers, from 10 to 280). This takes each trade up through its gates and asserts that the recipe of the next tier is not known one point below its gate and known at it. Refine Forestwood Plank and the three Forestwood intermediates are the client's own learned-on-skill-value rows and arrive with the trade, which is the shape the rest of the ladder takes.",
